  "comment": "Third-party binaries fetched into deps/ by scripts/fetch-deps.ps1, never committed. Each download is pinned by SHA256 (GitHub publishes a digest for every release asset). Change a version here, then run the script and the tests. 'notices' names every file the installer ships from deps/ and its licences (paths from the repository root); scripts/write-notices.ps1 refuses a file that has none. qpdf links zlib, libjpeg-turbo and OpenSSL into qpdf30.dll at whatever versions vcpkg had on the day of its build: after a qpdf update, pin their licences at the versions the binary holds (QpdfDepsTests checks). ffmpeg is pinned to the last BtbN build of a month, which BtbN keeps for two years (its daily builds go after 14 days). docs/adr/0008-pdf-engines-pdfium-and-qpdf.md, docs/adr/0009-ffmpeg-gpl-build.md, docs/adr/0010-tesseract-static-build.md",
